# Setup-success checklist — do not count onboarding import as done

**Symptom:** After finishing setup (or Get Started), **Invite and verify vendors** (or a similar step) never appears as incomplete — the landlord already “completed” it because vendors/residents were imported during onboarding.

**Cause:** Checklist `done` was tied to **roster presence** (`vendorCount > 0`, residents exist) instead of **manual outreach** (welcome text started / verification invite started). Onboarding does **not** auto-send SMS.

## Rule

| Checklist item | Done only when |
|---|---|
| `welcome_texts` | At least one resident has activation started (`activation_status` not empty / not `not_started`) — **not** merely imported with a phone |
| `verify_vendors` | At least one vendor has outreach started: any `vendor_verifications` row **or** `onboarding_overridden_at` — **not** merely `vendors` roster rows from import |

Mirror the product rule in `onboarding-auto-activation.mdc`: managers send outreach from Residents / Vendors when ready.

## Autofix (Bugbot)

On PR review or when a step is “done” right after Complete with only imported roster data:

1. Grep `resolveSetupSuccessProgress` / `loadSetupSuccessProgress` for `vendorCount > 0` (or similar) as the sole `verify_vendors` predicate — replace with `vendorOutreachStartedCount > 0` (invite/override).
2. Do not mark `welcome_texts` done from `residents.length` or phone present alone.
3. Keep coachmarks aligned: imported not-activated vendors → checkbox / Start onboarding guide; empty roster → Add vendor guide.
4. Add/keep a unit test: roster-only import → step **incomplete**; outreach started → **complete**.

**Note:** Cursor Bugbot runs on pull requests. Agents must apply this when the symptom appears in chat or PR.

## Where it lives

- Progress: `src/lib/setupSuccessChecklist.ts` → `resolveSetupSuccessProgress`
- Loader: `src/lib/loadSetupSuccessProgress.ts`
- Overview mirror: `AdminOverviewDashboard` progress input
- Vendors coachmark: `AdminVendorsDashboard`

## Do not

- Treat onboarding Fast Track / document import as completing invite or welcome-text steps
- Auto-send vendor/tenant SMS on `completeOnboarding` to “fix” the checklist
- Weaken the step by using roster count alone again
